# Overrides the image's own mods-enabled/mpm_prefork.conf entirely (same
# exact-path-replacement trick as z-deflate-disabled.conf, not the
# loads-after-alphabetically trick the z-nextcloud-*.conf files use - MPM
# config lives in mods-enabled under its own fixed filename, not somewhere
# ordering would help).
#
# The image's default MaxRequestWorkers (150) can exceed postgres_max_connections
# (currently {{ postgres_max_connections }}) under a big enough burst of
# concurrent requests - e.g. opening the Photos view against a library with
# no cached previews yet fires off many simultaneous preview-generation
# requests, each holding its own Postgres connection for the duration.
# Enough of them at once and Postgres starts rejecting new connections with
# "sorry, too many clients already" - confirmed live on this deployment.
# Capped well under postgres_max_connections here, leaving headroom for the
# cron sidecar and manual occ/admin sessions. Also just more appropriately
# sized for the actual CPU budget (nextcloud_cpus) - 150 concurrent workers
# was never going to run in real parallel on a couple of CPUs anyway; excess
# workers past that just contend for the same CPU time without adding
# throughput.
#
# prefork MPM
# StartServers: number of server processes to start
# MinSpareServers: minimum number of server processes which are kept spare
# MaxSpareServers: maximum number of server processes which are kept spare
# MaxRequestWorkers: maximum number of server processes allowed to start
# MaxConnectionsPerChild: maximum number of requests a server process serves

StartServers            5
MinSpareServers         5
MaxSpareServers         10
MaxRequestWorkers       {{ nextcloud_apache_max_workers | default('40') }}
MaxConnectionsPerChild  0
